    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Truly Unique Restored Thatched Cottage on c.16 Acres of Private Woodland\r\n\r\nOpportunities like this are exceptionally rare.\r\n\r\nProperty Partners McDonnell are proud to present \"Teach Duinn Shléibhe\", a beautifully restored stone thatched cottage that's been owned by the same family for over 275 years. Standing on approximately 16 acres of secluded mature woodland and forestry in one of County Westmeath's most peaceful and picturesque locations.\r\nHidden away at the end of a quiet country cul-de-sac, this enchanting property offers complete privacy while remaining just 1km from Castletown Geoghegan Village, 12 minutes from Mullingar, and only 5 minutes from the M6 motorway, making it the perfect balance of rural tranquility and modern convenience.\r\nLovingly restored over the years, the cottage retains many of its original character features including traditional flagstone flooring, wood-paneled ceilings, stable-style front door and an inviting solid fuel stove that creates a warm and welcoming atmosphere.\r\nThe accommodation comprises a spacious sitting room, fully fitted country-style kitchen/dining room, utility room, ground floor shower room and three charming first-floor bedrooms, each enjoying delightful views over the surrounding countryside and woodland.\r\nOutside, the property offers an outstanding collection of traditional stone outbuildings including former stables, cow byres, pump house, workshop and fuel store, providing excellent potential for hobby farming, equestrian enthusiasts, artists, craftspeople or a wide variety of lifestyle uses (subject to any necessary planning permission).\r\nThe surrounding woodland, planted approximately 20 years ago with mainly Alder and Beech trees, creates a magical natural setting rich in wildlife and offers endless opportunities for walking, recreation or simply enjoying the peace and beauty of your own private forest.\r\nWhether you're seeking a unique family home, country retreat, hobby farm, holiday residence or investment in a truly special property, \"Teach Duinn Shléibhe\" is a home that simply cannot be replicated.\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the charm, privacy and lifestyle this remarkable property has to offer.\r\n\r\nPrice Guide: €595,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Sitting Room\r\n4.681m x 6.882m\r\nLarge Open Plan room retaining a lot of the Cottages Original Features. Flag Stone Flooring. Wood Paneled Ceiling. Solid Fuel Wood Burning Stove. Door to rear & Kitchen off Living Room. “Stable Style” Front Door\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room\r\n3.746m x 5.076m\r\nFully Fitted Wall & Floor Kitchen Units with counter top, tiled Splash Back and delph sink unit. Integrated Electric Oven & ceramic hob. Plumbed for washing machine. \r\n\r\nInner Hall\r\n2.478m x 1.560m\r\nUnder Stair Storage cupboard. Spot lights on Ceiling. \r\n\r\nUtility Room\r\n2.365m x 1.911m\r\nFlag Stone Flooring. Built-In Shelving & Door to rear.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom\r\n1.905m x 3.296m\r\nFlag stone Floor. Newly tiled walls. WC., WHB., Raised Bath and Shower Cubicle. Window for Natural Ventilation. Window allowing for natural lighting and ventilation. Ceiling extractor fan. \r\n\r\nLanding\r\n5.144m x 1.513m\r\nNew laminate flooring & Wood Paneled Ceiling.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n2.625m x 3.380m\r\nDouble Dormer Room. Side & Rear Aspect. New Laminate Flooring. 2 Windows. TV Point. Radiator. Spotlight on Ceiling. 2 Double sockets.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n3.103m x 2.255m\r\nDouble Dormer Room. Rear Aspect. Access to Attic. New Laminate Flooring. Radiator. Window to Rear. Wood Paneled Ceiling. Hot-press off with Shelving.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nDouble Dormer Room. Rear & Side Aspect. Carpet Flooring. Radiator. Wood Paneled Ceiling.\r\n\r\nOUTBUILDINGS:\r\nDetached Stone Outbuilding consisting of: \r\nPump House\r\n2.293m x 2.954m\r\nPump House and holds Oil fired central heating boiler.  Double Door access.\r\n\r\nShed No.2 (Attached to Pump House)\r\n4.083m x 5.399m\r\nCow Byre. Concrete floor. Old Built-In feed trough. Front & Rear door access. Power Point.\r\n\r\nShed No.3 (Lean-to off Pump/Boiler House)\r\n3.619m x 4.025m\r\nOpen Window for ventilation. Walled division\r\n\r\nStable 1\r\n3.261m 3.325m\r\nOld Style Cobble lock floor with door access.\r\n\r\nStable 2\r\n2.398m 3.532m\r\nOld Style Cobble lock floors with stable door\r\n\r\nStable 3\r\n2.388m 3.532m\r\nOld Style Cobble lock floors with stable door\r\n\r\nOpen Plan Fuel Shed\r\n3.599m x 8.416m\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nDetached stone outbuildings\r\nFormer stables\r\nPump house\r\nWorkshop\r\nFuel shed\r\nExtensive parking\r\nGated entrance\r\nMature gardens and woodland"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Authentic restored thatched stone cottage \r\nApprox. 16 acres of mature woodland and forestry\r\nPrivate and secluded end-of-road setting\r\nOil fired central heating\r\nSolid fuel stove\r\nOriginal character features throughout\r\nExcellent range of traditional stone outbuildings\r\nHuge potential for equestrian, hobby farming or lifestyle use\r\nPrivate well and septic tank\r\nForestry planted approximately 20 years ago\r\nOnly 1km from Castletown Geoghegan Village\r\nApproximately 12 minutes to Mullingar Town\r\nEasy access to the M6 motorway\r\nViewing strictly by appointment"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: Exempt"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "Castletown Geoghegan is one of Westmeath's most sought-after rural villages, renowned for its welcoming community, excellent primary school and beautiful countryside.\r\nNearby attractions include Lough Ennell, Lough Owel, Lough Derravaragh, Belvedere House & Gardens, the River Brosna, and the Mullingar–Athlone Greenway, offering an exceptional lifestyle for outdoor enthusiasts. Mullingar provides an extensive range of shopping, restaurants, cafés, schools and sporting facilities, while Dublin is within comfortable commuting distance via the nearby M6."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
        "SortOrder": 6,
        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only"
      }
